<section data-state="rec">
    <h3>Pick the tests with PHPUnit</h3>
    <pre><code class="language-bash" data-trim>
# record a class again after an API change
SYMFONY_HTTP_RECORDER=record vendor/bin/phpunit --filter GetRandomControllerTest

# add what is missing in a group, without touching the rest
SYMFONY_HTTP_RECORDER=missing vendor/bin/phpunit --group payment
    </code></pre>
    <div class="card-row">
        <div class="card amber fragment">
            <h4>Why not in the attribute?</h4>
            <p>A recording mode must never be committed: it is a setting for the duration of a run.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card green fragment">
            <h4>Before committing</h4>
            <p>Review the diff of the HAR files, like any other code.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="notes">
        <p>And to choose which tests to record, we didn't invent anything: we use what PHPUnit already does. --filter, --group, a path. Here, we record a class again after an API change, and we add what's missing in the payment group without touching the rest.</p>
        <p>[click] Why not put the mode in the attribute? Because a recording mode must never be committed: you turn it on for one run, whereas the attribute is part of the test.</p>
        <p>[click] Then we review the diff of the .har files. And that diff is precious: it shows you in black and white what changed in the API.</p>
    </aside>
</section>
